<item><title>Health experts seek more climate funding for Africa’s malaria response</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/et/health-experts-seek-more-climate-funding-for-africa-s-c2a162/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/et/health-experts-seek-more-climate-funding-for-africa-s-c2a162/</guid><category>Ethiopia</category><description>The Roll Back Malaria Partnership says health gets only 6% of climate finance, despite rising pressure on health systems and medicine delivery.</description><pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 04:06:52 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/et.jpg" length="32890" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/et.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Ethiopia’s central bank holds forex supply at $140 million as bids exceed it</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/et/ethiopia-s-central-bank-holds-forex-supply-at-140-million-957365/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/et/ethiopia-s-central-bank-holds-forex-supply-at-140-million-957365/</guid><category>Ethiopia</category><description>Banks bid $160.76 million on November 24, while the birr’s marginal rate rose to 159.40 per dollar from 159.18 at the previous auction.</description><pubDate>Tue, 24 Nov 2026 19:30:44 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/et/ethiopia-s-central-bank-holds-forex-supply-at-140-million-957365/share.jpg" length="42822" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/et/ethiopia-s-central-bank-holds-forex-supply-at-140-million-957365/share.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Abiy offers to host inclusive talks on Sudan war</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/et/abiy-offers-to-host-inclusive-talks-on-sudan-war-fc8587/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/et/abiy-offers-to-host-inclusive-talks-on-sudan-war-fc8587/</guid><category>Ethiopia</category><description>Ethiopia invited Sudan’s military, political and civilian groups to negotiations, and two Sudanese factions welcomed the proposal on Tuesday.</description><pubDate>Tue, 24 Nov 2026 17:16:30 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/et.jpg" length="32890" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/et.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
